    "en": {
      "trackName": "Wrist Chess Hall: Watch Games",
      "description": "Wrist Chess Hall is an offline board game collection designed for iPhone, iPad, and Apple Watch.\nStep into a watercolor-inspired game hall and choose from four classic games:\n• Chinese Chess: Casual rules with check, horse-leg, elephant-eye, cannon-screen, palace, and river rules.\n• Gomoku: Play on 9×9 or 13×13 boards.\n• Reversi: Choose 6×6 or 8×8 boards with automatic pass handling.\n• Tic-Tac-Toe: A quick game for a short break.\nThe app includes:\n• Offline games against the computer\n• Beginner, Advanced, and Challenge difficulty levels\n• Two-player games on one device\n• First-player and second-player options\n• Full-screen board layout on Apple Watch\n• Automatic save and resume\n• Undo, hints, move confirmation, and legal move hints\n• Sound effects and haptic feedback\n• No account, ads, or internet connection required\nGames are stored locally on the current device. iPhone and Apple Watch keep separate saved games.\nWhat’s New\nFirst release: Chinese Chess, Gomoku, Reversi, and Tic-Tac-Toe with offline play on iPhone, iPad, and Apple Watch.",
      "releaseNotes": "• Discover Flip Chess: reveal 32 randomly placed, face-down Chinese chess pieces. Take turns revealing, moving, and capturing.\n• Equal-ranked opponents eliminate each other, while pawns can capture generals—small pieces can make a big difference.\n• Enjoy a new capture sound for Flip Chess, shared by player and AI moves, including equal-rank trades.\n• Improved end-of-game audio timing so the capture sound finishes before the final chime.",
