    {
      "version": "1.1",
      "releaseNotes": "• Zoom the board on Apple Watch by turning the Digital Crown. Drag to explore the board when zoomed in.\n• The app icon label now displays “Wrist Chess Hall” when your device language is set to English.",
      "seenAt": "2026-09-23T11:22:12Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "1.2",
      "releaseNotes": "Meet Wolves & Sheep! Enjoy a strategic battle of three wolves against nine sheep—capture sheep or work together to trap the wolves. Discover a new meadow theme with charming animal pieces. Play offline against AI or share a device with a friend, with undo, hints, and automatic game saving. Available on iPhone, iPad, and Apple Watch in nine languages.",
      "seenAt": "2026-10-02T00:15:49Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "1.3",
      "releaseNotes": "• Introducing Flip Chess! Reveal 32 randomly placed, face-down Chinese chess pieces. Take turns revealing, moving, or capturing as you plan your next move.\n• Discover unique capture rules: higher ranks capture lower ranks, pawns can capture generals, and equal-ranked opponents eliminate each other.\n• Play against AI or take turns with a friend on the same device, with undo and saved games.\n• Enjoy Flip Chess on iPhone, iPad, and Apple Watch.",
      "seenAt": "2026-10-03T21:16:10Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "1.4",
      "releaseNotes": "• Discover Flip Chess: reveal 32 randomly placed, face-down Chinese chess pieces. Take turns revealing, moving, and capturing.\n• Equal-ranked opponents eliminate each other, while pawns can capture generals—small pieces can make a big difference.\n• Enjoy a new capture sound for Flip Chess, shared by player and AI moves, including equal-rank trades.\n• Improved end-of-game audio timing so the capture sound finishes before the final chime.",
      "seenAt": "2026-10-04T21:51:52Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "1.5",
      "releaseNotes": "• Introducing Wolves & Sheep II: a new stone board where wolves leap across empty points to capture sheep, while sheep work together to trap them.\n• The original game is now Wolves & Sheep I, with its gameplay and saved games preserved.\n• Improved Apple Watch layout: Back and Undo now sit at the top, with fewer on-screen labels and more room for the board.\n• Wolves & Sheep II now uses the same capture sound as Flip Chess.\n• Updated game names, instructions, and interface text across nine languages.",
      "seenAt": "2026-10-09T15:26:26Z"
    }
  ],
